 ],
 "notes": "null-label module wiring is not visible to the adapter (only variables); checked loosely via standard context variables. The prompt does not give default_security_group_deny_all a default, so the default SG is accepted as declared and the variable is checked by name only. Stripping all rules: the default SG (planned, or declared) carries no static ingress/egress blocks; a declared SG whose dynamic blocks add rules is accepted by the declared branch (rare encoding). IPAM/netmask/timeout support is checked on declared (default-off) association resources; a single-expression variable reference is resolved to its (null) default in __declared__, so the primary IPAM support also accepts an IPAM variable. Additional CIDR associations must be declared gated (for_each over the map variable), so a single hardcoded association fails. The route-table/NACL adoption flags are checked as gated declarations; the stated false defaults are not checked separately because the prompt does not name those variables."
}